      "description": "## Overview\n[uri-js](https://github.com/garycourt/uri-js) is a RFC 3986/3987 compliant, scheme extendable URI/IRI parsing/validating/resolving library for JavaScript.\n\nAffected versions of this package are vulnerable to Uncaught Exception in the `parse()` function of `src/schemes/mailto.ts`, whose `to` branch calls `hfield[1].split(\",\")` directly, while the `subject`, `body`, and default branches all route through `unescapeComponent()`, which short-circuits on a missing value. An attacker can crash the process by supplying a mailto URI whose query carries a bare `to` token with no `=value`, such as `mailto:?to`, so splitting on `=` yields a one element array and the undefined second element is dereferenced. This requires the application to pass an attacker-influenced string to `URI.parse()`, `URI.resolve()`, `URI.normalize()`, or `URI.equal()`, none of which wrap the scheme handler in a `try`/`catch`, and whether the throw terminates the process or only fails the one request depends on the host's own error handling.\n## Remediation\nThere is no fixed version for `uri-js`.\n## References\n- [GitHub Issue](https://github.com/garycourt/uri-js/issues/103)\n",
